  "id": "Compound::DB01019 - Gene::1131",
  "verbalization": "Bethanechol, a cholinergic agonist, is known to bind to muscarinic acetylcholine receptors (Muscarinic Acetylcholine Receptors), which are a subset of G-protein coupled receptors. This binding activates a series of downstream signaling pathways, including the G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity. The evidence from the visible paths suggests that Bethanechol interacts with Chrm2, a muscarinic receptor, which in turn participates in the G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptor activity. This pathway ultimately leads to the participation of Chrm3 in the same activity. The consistent binding of Bethanechol to Chrm2 and the subsequent activation of G-protein coupled receptor activity provide a mechanistic link between the drug and Chrm3. The evidence is supported by multiple paths with high scores, indicating a robust and well-documented interaction. The mechanism involves the activation of muscarinic receptors, which then trigger G-protein signaling, leading to the activation of Chrm3. This pathway is biologically plausible and aligns with known cholinergic receptor function.",
